WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:08.790
With just one year to go, anticipation is
building across the District as Stadium Waimakariri

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.600
starts to take shape.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.020
The Mayor and Councillors toured the site
last week alongside staff from the North Canterbury

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.360
Sport &amp; Recreation Trust who will be responsible
for managing the facility

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.520
once construction is complete.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.720
Mayor Dan Gordon says it was wonderful to
be able to walk through the building and get

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.320
a sense of what the finished Stadium will
be like.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.640
It's really good to come through and have a
sneak preview of where this project is at.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.750
As we can see a lot of people have been talking
about it as they've gone past on Coldstream

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.560
Road and seen the framing go up.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.960
It's looking fantastic, I understand it's
well on track and the contractors are certainly

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.660
making a good job of it as we can see.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.220
It's going to be a terrific asset to our community
this facility.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:02.220
Four courts with all the other services that
will be here including a gymnasium as well.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.140
So it's good to see progress and it's good
see the contractors are doing such a good

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.580
job on behalf of our community.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:15.560
The $28 million multi-use sports facility
will be approximately 6,000 square metres

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:21.580
in size and house four indoor courts, as well
as a central fitness facility, changing rooms,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:26.520
coaching and meeting spaces and seating for
up to 500 spectators.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.140
Designed by Warren and Mahoney architects,
it aims to become a vibrant focus point for

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.920
sport in the District.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.140
The Stadium can also easily be expanded in
the future if required.

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:43.609
The site on Coldstream Road places it near
other sporting grounds such as the MainPower

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:47.020
Oval, MainPower Hockey Turf and Maria Andrews
Park.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.880
Despite a small delay due to the Covid-19
lockdown, construction is on schedule.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.640
It’s expected that the Stadium’s doors
will open to the public towards the end of July 2021.

